# Inflected forms that must KEEP their dictionary rank, subtracted from ja.demoted on every
# regeneration. Format: reading<TAB>surface.
#
# The heuristic is right that these are inflections; demoting them is still wrong, for one of two
# reasons. Either the form has lexicalised into a word of its own (向こう is a noun, "the other
# side", not a reading of 向く), or it is so much commoner than anything else under its reading
# that the promotion is a downgrade — including the rows whose only rival is corpus junk.
#
# Each line names what WOULD lead the reading if the form were demoted.

# --- lexicalised: no longer felt as an inflection
むこう	向こう	# would promote 無効

# --- far commoner than the rival
よく	良く	# would promote 翌, which is a bound prefix, not a word
たいし	対し	# would promote 太子
まとう	待とう	# would promote 纏う

# --- the only rival is corpus junk
いえよう	言えよう	# would promote 家用
うえん	植えん	# would promote う炎
なめん	舐めん	# would promote な面
